Z||000000||Alex4mula||07-20-2001||09:02 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.chrfab.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.chrfab.com</A> <P>It is mentioned on current HotRod mag that this place has headers, wire harness, etc. for N* engines. Their website shows some very nice intake manifolds.  Just passing the info for those of you interested in that swap.<BR><P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red & White (:<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p69fbfe3e99ec5a0b81c10afcc578ff95/fe6d5c42.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||07-20-2001||01:03 PM||||They also stock stand-alone ECMs.<BR>Pricey, though.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.chrfab.com/Ignitions.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.chrfab.com/Ignitions.htm</A> <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||artherd||07-22-2001||08:52 PM||||Actually, $1300 for an ECM *AND* wiring harness for an engine so complex (well, compared to the "stick the hose in the intake and spark it with flint" sect :) I think it's a pretty good deal actually.<P>The "hemi" valve covers are just cool, heheh!<P>(PS: these chrfab guys rule, hotrodding for the 21st centuary. Really.)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000003||Formula88||07-23-2001||09:14 AM||||Yeah, these guys are actually making me lean towards a N* conversion.  Just gotta make sure it can be done, reliably, with a Getrag, otherwise I'd just use a SBC.||||reg||10
Z||000004||Raydar||07-23-2001||09:26 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<BR><B>Actually, $1300 for an ECM *AND* wiring harness for an engine so complex (well, compared to the "stick the hose in the intake and spark it with flint" sect   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I think it's a pretty good deal actually.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Of course you're right. <BR>I was just speaking in relative terms, compared to swapping in a 3800 and it's ECM, and piecing together a harness. <BR>I suspect that when you consider the entire scope of a N* swap, $1300 for an ECM that you don't have to re-engineer is pretty reasonable. <P>Not that I have ever attempted either one.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 07-23-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000005||Wannabe||07-23-2001||09:58 AM||||Around here, and I'd imagine most other areas, Northstars are a dime a dozen. You can easily pick up a low mileage (30-40K miles) Northstar for C$1200-1500. Adding the CHRFab controller to that makes is about $2400 for a running N* with controller. Sounds very reasonable!||||reg||1
Z||000006||artherd||07-23-2001||03:53 PM||||We'll see when I'm done, but the cost is going to end up being about what I'd pay for a well-done injected LT1/zz4 350 swap.<P>There are several concerns about reliability, all of them based on conjecture.  Will and I will see for real! :)  It may be a kitten or it may blow up after a few days.   But we'll be essentially the first with hard, imperical data :)<P>True, $1300 is more than the ECU that you could grab from a junkyard, but keep in mind these are new parts, and at that, essentially custom engineered racing parts, and give you total 3D fuel map control from a laptop (pretty cool! like what those guys in Fast and the Furrious paid $10,000+ for :)  <P>Anyway, chrfab has cams for the northstar too....  (now I want them to start stocking the LMR bits, specially the 4000cc 180 crank and fordged superlight bits. hehhe :)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
